---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { RecordListPlayground } from '../../components/RecordListDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Record List"
  description="Rows of records to read and triage, with labelled values, badges, and row actions."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Record List</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The List view of a table. Each record on the current page is one row: a title, up to four labelled values, choice
    badges, and row actions. Use it to read and triage records. Use Table to compare values in columns, edit, or select
    rows in bulk.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <RecordListPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A page of tickets"
      code={`import { Badge } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/badge";
import { RecordList, type RecordListHandle } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/record-list";

const list = useRef<RecordListHandle>(null);

<RecordList
  ref={list}
  label="Tickets"
  items={page.rows}
  status={read.loading ? "loading" : read.failed ? "error" : "ready"}
  onRetry={read.retry}
  values={(ticket) => [
    { label: "Assignee", value: ticket.assignee },
    { label: "Due", value: ticket.due },
  ]}
  badges={(ticket) => <Badge variant="info">{ticket.status}</Badge>}
  renderActions={(ticket) => <TicketActions ticket={ticket} />}
  onItemOpen={(ticket) => openSheet(ticket)}
  footer={<TicketPagination onPageChange={() => list.current?.focusFirst()} />}
/>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>items</code>: <code>{'{ id, title }[]'}</code> plus your own fields, in page order.
        <code>title</code> is plain text. Screen readers use it, and it shows in full on hover.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>label</code> names the list. The row count is added, so screen readers hear “Tickets, 6 rows”.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>renderTitle</code> draws the title, such as a key before the text. Screen readers still use
        <code>title</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>values</code> returns <code>{'{ label, value, text? }[]'}</code>.{' '}
        <strong>Only the first four show; the rest are left out.</strong> Leave out empty values before you return them.
        Use <code>text</code> for the hover hint when
        <code>value</code> is not a string or number.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>badges</code> returns choice badges, such as status and priority. Leave out empty choices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>renderActions</code> is a free slot for row actions, such as an Edit icon button and a
        <code>DropdownMenu</code>. Clicks in it never open the row. Give each action a name that includes the row.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>onItemOpen</code> runs on a click anywhere else in the row, or on Enter. A click that ends a text
        selection does not open the row.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>footer</code> sits under the rows inside the panel. Put your <code>Pagination</code> there.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>density="compact"</code> uses 8px by 12px padding instead of 12px by 16px.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      <code>status</code> is <code>"ready"</code>, <code>"loading"</code>, or <code>"error"</code>. While a page loads
      and rows are already shown, they stay in place, dimmed, with <code>aria-busy</code> and a “Loading rows…”
      announcement. With no rows yet, five skeleton rows hold the space.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>"error"</code> replaces the rows with an error state. <code>error</code> is its description, and
      <code>onRetry</code> adds a Try again button. When <code>items</code> is empty and ready, the list shows
      <code>empty</code>: pass a <code>StatePanel</code> or text. Without it, the list says “No rows to show”.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Custom empty state"
      code={`<RecordList
  label="Tickets"
  items={[]}
  empty={
    <StatePanel kind="empty" heading="h3" title="No rows match" description="No tickets match the current filters.">
      <Button variant="outline" onClick={clearFilters}>Clear filters</Button>
    </StatePanel>
  }
/>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Layout</h2>
    <p>
      Rows sit in one bordered panel, separated by hairlines. The title is on the first line in 14px medium text. Values
      follow on the second line as muted label and strong value pairs, with tabular numerals, 16px apart, wrapping as
      needed. Badges and actions sit on the right.
    </p>
    <p>
      Long titles cut off after one line. Each value cuts off at 16rem. The full text shows on hover and is always read
      by screen readers. When the list is 640px wide or less, badges move under the values, actions stay at the top
      right, and titles wrap to two lines.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Keyboard and focus</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The list is one tab stop. Tab lands on the last focused row, or the first row.</li>
      <li>Up and Down move between rows. Home and End go to the first and last row. Enter opens the row.</li>
      <li>
        Tab from a row reaches that row's actions, then leaves the list. Actions in other rows are out of the tab order
        until their row is focused. Clicking an action also makes its row the focused row.
      </li>
      <li>
        Menus opened from actions work as usual, and focus returns to their trigger when they close. Shift+Tab from an
        action goes back to its row.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      After a page change, call <code>focusFirst()</code> on the ref so focus does not fall to the page. While
      <code>status</code> is <code>"loading"</code>, it waits for the new rows, so you can call it from the page
      button's click handler. With no rows, it focuses the empty or error state.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The list is a named <code>list</code>, and each row is a <code>listitem</code> named by its title. The values and
      badges describe the row, so screen readers read them after the title. Values are a description list of field and
      value. Rows have a hover color and an inset focus ring. Rows fade in over 180ms and the dim changes smoothly only
      when reduced motion is not requested. In forced colors mode the lines use the system text color.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The panel uses <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, and <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code>.
      Titles and values use <code>--sprout-text</code>, labels use <code>--sprout-muted</code>, and hover uses
      <code>--sprout-hover</code>. Focus uses <code>--sprout-focus-ring</code> and <code>--sprout-focus-width</code>.
      Motion uses <code>--sprout-motion-fast</code>, <code>--sprout-motion-normal</code>, and
      <code>--sprout-motion-ease</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
